<title>POLAND: Budimex shareholders approve merger.</title>
<headline>Budimex shareholders approve merger.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish construction company Budimex SA shareholders approved on Tuesday a merger with its former subsidiary Budimex Trading SA, Budimex SA said in a statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The merger would be carried out by Budimex SA taking all the assets of Budimex Trading.</p>
<p>Budimex said it would issue two million registered, preferred shares for Budimex Trading SA shareholders and said that two shares in Budimex Trading would be exchanged for one Budimex SA new share.</p>
<p>Each of the new Budimex SA's shares would carry five voting rights.</p>
<p>Budimex Trading SA main shareholder is Kredyt Bank SA with a 56-percent stake and the remaining shareholders have stakes of below five percent.</p>
<p>Budimex Trading shares will later be retired.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
